          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Other Side of Zero"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.12,
            0.301,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.15,
            0.833,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Try to subtract: – 3 – (+ 5). How many zero pairs will you have to put in? What is the result?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.196,
            0.761,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Evaluate the following using tokens. a. (– 3) – (+ 10) b. (+ 8) – (– 7) c. (– 5) – (+ 9) d. (– 9) – (+ 10) e. (+ 6) – (– 4) f. (– 2) – (+ 7)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.289,
            0.537,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.3 Integers in Other Places"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.336,
            0.334,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Credits and debits"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.366,
            0.834,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose you open a bank account at your local bank with the `100 that you had been saving over the last month. Your bank balance therefore, starts at `100."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.441,
            0.833,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Then you make `60 at your job the next day and you deposit it in your account. This is shown in your bank passbook as a ‘credit’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.493,
            0.502,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Your new bank balance is __"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.528,
            0.833,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The next day you pay your electric bill of `30 using your bank account. This is shown in your bank passbook as a ‘debit’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.586,
            0.492,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Your bank balance is now ______."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.623,
            0.834,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The next day you make a major purchase for your business of `150. Again this is shown as a debit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.68,
            0.569,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is your bank balance now?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.716,
            0.33,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is this possible?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.757,
            0.835,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yes, some banks do allow your account balance to become negative, temporarily! Some banks also charge you an additional amount if your balance becomes negative, in the form of ‘interest’ or a ‘fee’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.839,
            0.833,
            0.884
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Your strategic large purchase the previous day allows you to make, `200 at your business the next day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
